1
00:02:22,010 --> 00:02:25,060
- Does Ser Hugh have any family in the capital? - No.

2
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:29,690
I stood vigil for him myself last night.

3
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,120
He had no one else.

4
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:35,810
He'd never worn this armor before.

5
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:38,330
Bad luck for him...

6
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:40,090
going against the Mountain.

7
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,530
Who determines the draw?

8
00:02:43,170 --> 00:02:45,410
All the knights draw straws, Lord Stark.

9
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:46,540
Aye.

10
00:02:47,330 --> 00:02:49,290
But who holds the straws?

11
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:53,290
You've done good work, sisters.

12
00:02:58,670 --> 00:03:01,630
Life is strange. Not so many years ago

13
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:03,620
we fought as enemies at the Trident.

14
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:06,800
I'm glad we never met on the field, Ser Barristan.

15
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,780
As is my wife.

16
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:10,840
I don't think the widow's life would suit her.

17
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:12,850
You're too modest.

18
00:03:12,850 --> 00:03:15,170
I've seen you cut down a dozen great knights.

19
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:16,800
My father once told me

20
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:18,400
you were the best he'd ever seen.

21
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:22,240
I never knew the man to be wrong about matters of combat.

22
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:24,290
He was a fine man, your father.

23
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:27,790
What the Mad King did to him was a terrible crime.

24
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:29,160
And that lad...

25
00:03:29,670 --> 00:03:31,590
He was a squire until a few months ago.

26
00:03:31,590 --> 00:03:33,670
How could he afford a new suit of armor?

27
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:36,550
Perhaps Lord Arryn left him some money?

28
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:40,710
I hear the king wants to joust today.

29
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:42,700
Yes, that will never happen.

30
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:45,330
Robert tends to do what he wants.

31
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:47,610
If the king got what he wanted all the time,

32
00:03:47,910 --> 00:03:50,160
he'd still be fighting a damned rebellion.

33
00:03:55,430 --> 00:03:57,920
It's made too small, your Grace. It won't go.

34
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:02,950
Your mother was a dumb whore with a fat ass. Did you know that?

35
00:04:05,490 --> 00:04:09,140
Look at this idiot! One ball and no brains.

36
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:12,010
He can't even put a man's armor on him properly.

37
00:04:12,010 --> 00:04:13,800
You're too fat for your armor.

38
00:04:13,810 --> 00:04:17,370
Fat? Fat, is it?

39
00:04:17,550 --> 00:04:20,120
Is that how you speak to your king?

40
00:04:27,790 --> 00:04:29,320
That was funny, is it?

41
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,760
No, your Grace.

42
00:04:32,870 --> 00:04:36,270
No? You don't like the Hand's joke?

43
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:39,110
You're torturing the poor boy.

44
00:04:39,110 --> 00:04:41,910
You heard the Hand. The king's too fat for his armor.

45
00:04:41,910 --> 00:04:45,260
Go find the breastplate stretcher... Now!

46
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:49,710
"The breastplate stretcher"?

47
00:04:50,110 --> 00:04:52,390
How long before he figures it out?

48
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,750
- Maybe you should have one invented. - All right, all right.

49
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:58,510
But you watch me out there... I still know how to point a lance.

50
00:04:58,510 --> 00:05:01,730
You have no business jousting. Leave that for the young men.

51
00:05:01,730 --> 00:05:05,060
Why, because I'm king? Piss on that. I want to hit somebody!

52
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:07,450
- And who's going to hit you back? - Anybody who can.

53
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:09,790
- And the last man in his saddle... - Will be you.

54
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:12,340
There's not a man in the Seven Kingdoms

55
00:05:12,340 --> 00:05:13,890
would risk hurting you.

56
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:17,210
Are you telling me those cowards would let me win?

57
00:05:17,210 --> 00:05:18,230
Aye.

58
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,830
- Drink. - I'm not thirsty.

59
00:05:26,830 --> 00:05:29,390
Drink. Your king commands it.

60
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:34,540
Gods,

61
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:37,600
too fat for my armor.

62
00:05:38,530 --> 00:05:41,280
Your squire... A Lannister boy?

63
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,830
Mm. A bloody idiot,

64
00:05:43,830 --> 00:05:45,890
but Cersei insisted.

65
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:49,250
I have Jon Arryn to thank for her.

66
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:52,910
"Cersei Lannister will make a good match," He told me.

67
00:05:52,910 --> 00:05:55,520
"You'll need her father on your side."

68
00:05:56,920 --> 00:06:00,860
I thought being king meant I could do whatever I wanted.

69
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,420
Enough of this. Let's go watch 'em ride.

70
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:09,020
At least I can smell someone else's blood.

71
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:10,810
- Robert? - What?

72
00:06:14,790 --> 00:06:17,430
An inspiring sight for the people, eh?

73
00:06:17,430 --> 00:06:21,440
Come, bow before your king! Bow, you shits!

74
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:37,690
- Where's Arya? - At her dancing lessons.

75
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,590
The Knight of the Flowers.

76
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:51,040
Thank you, Ser Loras.

77
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:24,400
Don't let Ser Gregor hurt him.

78
00:07:25,770 --> 00:07:27,650
I can't watch.

79
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:32,800
100 gold dragons on the Mountain.

80
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:33,970
I'll take that bet.

81
00:07:33,970 --> 00:07:36,670
Now what will I buy with 100 gold dragons?

82
00:07:36,670 --> 00:07:38,950
A dozen barrels of Dornish wine?

83
00:07:38,990 --> 00:07:42,060
Or a girl from the pleasure houses of Lys?

84
00:07:42,060 --> 00:07:43,440
Or you could even buy a friend.

85
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:45,710
He's going to die.

86
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:47,780
Ser Loras rides well.

87
00:08:17,890 --> 00:08:20,030
Such a shame, Littlefinger.

88
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:22,480
It would have been so nice for you to have a friend.

89
00:08:23,730 --> 00:08:25,500
And tell me, Lord Renly,

90
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:28,450
when will you be having your friend?

91
00:08:38,930 --> 00:08:40,840
Loras knew his mare was in heat.

92
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,460
Quite crafty, really.

93
00:08:43,090 --> 00:08:44,830
Ser Loras would never do that.

94
00:08:44,830 --> 00:08:46,050
There's no honor in tricks.

95
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:48,520
No honor and quite a bit of gold.

96
00:08:51,450 --> 00:08:52,650
Sword!

97
00:09:18,230 --> 00:09:19,540
Leave him be!

98
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:45,430
Stop this madness in the name of your king!

99
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:52,260
Let him go!

100
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:03,080
I owe you my life, ser.

101
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:05,390
I'm no ser.

102
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:31,280
Remove his hood.

103
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:34,320
On that eve, the captive Imp

104
00:10:34,470 --> 00:10:37,620
Downwards from his horse did limp

105
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:40,870
No more would he preen and primp

106
00:10:41,130 --> 00:10:44,070
- in garb of red and gold. - This isn't the Kingsroad.

107
00:10:44,070 --> 00:10:45,510
You said we were riding for Winterfell.

108
00:10:45,510 --> 00:10:48,670
I did... often and loudly.

109
00:10:48,670 --> 00:10:50,010
Very wise.

110
00:10:50,670 --> 00:10:52,280
They'll be out in droves,

111
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:54,440
looking for me in the wrong place.

112
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:57,080
Word's probably gotten to my father by now.

113
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:59,990
He'll be offering a handsome reward.

114
00:11:00,070 --> 00:11:03,370
Everyone knows a Lannister always pays his debts.

115
00:11:03,790 --> 00:11:06,240
Would you be so good as to untie me?

116
00:11:06,510 --> 00:11:09,190
- And why would I do that? - Why not?

117
00:11:09,190 --> 00:11:10,760
Am I going to run?

118
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:12,880
The hill tribes would kill me for my boots.

119
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,670
Unless a shadowcat ate me first.

120
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:18,270
Shadowcats and hill tribes are the least of your concerns.

121
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:21,970
Ah, the eastern road.

122
00:11:22,270 --> 00:11:24,200
We're going to the Vale.

123
00:11:24,370 --> 00:11:26,120
You're taking me to your sister's

124
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:28,000
to answer for my imagined crimes.

125
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,070
Tell me, Lady Stark,

126
00:11:29,070 --> 00:11:31,610
when was the last time you saw your sister?

127
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:33,700
Five years ago.

128
00:11:33,710 --> 00:11:35,260
She's changed.

129
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:38,320
She was always a bit touched, but now...

130
00:11:38,330 --> 00:11:39,860
you might as well kill me here.

131
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:43,160
- I am not a murderer, Lannister. - Neither am I!

132
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:45,480
I had nothing to do with the attempt on your son's life.

133
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:47,480
- The dagger found... - What sort of imbecile

134
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:49,650
arms an assassin with his own blade?

135
00:11:49,650 --> 00:11:51,860
- Should I gag him? - Why?

136
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:53,750
Am I starting to make sense?

137
00:11:55,650 --> 00:11:56,730
Rodrik!

138
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,270
My lady, this way.

139
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:19,580
Untie me.

140
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:22,220
If I die, what's the point?

141
00:13:14,230 --> 00:13:15,300
Rodrik?

142
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,490
I'll be fine, my lady.

143
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:19,670
There's no need to bloody yourself.

144
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:22,450
Your first?

145
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:25,730
You need a woman.

146
00:13:26,850 --> 00:13:28,900
Nothing like a woman after a fight.

147
00:13:31,090 --> 00:13:33,090
I'm willing if she is.

148
00:13:45,900 --> 00:13:47,060
Bran.

149
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,540
The Iron Islands.

150
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,410
Sigil: a kraken.

151
00:13:51,410 --> 00:13:53,770
Words: We do not sow.

152
00:13:53,810 --> 00:13:55,870
- Lords? - The Greyjoys.

153
00:13:55,870 --> 00:13:59,620
Famed for their skills at archery, navigation and lovemaking.

154
00:14:01,070 --> 00:14:03,040
And failed rebellions.

155
00:14:05,310 --> 00:14:06,990
Sigil: a stag...

156
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,660
a crowned stag now that Robert's king.

157
00:14:09,660 --> 00:14:13,040
- Good. - Words: Ours is the fury.

158
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:15,520
Lords: the Baratheons.

159
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:17,400
The Westerlands.

160
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:19,740
Sigil: a lion.

161
00:14:19,750 --> 00:14:23,200
- Words: A Lannister always pays his debts. - No.

162
00:14:23,370 --> 00:14:26,300
A common saying, but not their official motto.

163
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:28,860
Lords: the Lannisters.

164
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:31,710
- We're still on their words. - I don't know them.

165
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:33,600
You do know them. Think.

166
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:36,160
"Unbowed, unbent, unbroken."

167
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:38,890
- That's house Martell. - "Righteous in wrath."

168
00:14:38,890 --> 00:14:42,450
- House Hornwood. - "Family, duty, honor."

169
00:14:42,670 --> 00:14:44,700
Those are Tully words... your mother's.

170
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:48,140
- Are we playing a game? - Family, duty, honor...

171
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:50,590
- Is that the right order? - You know it is.

172
00:14:50,590 --> 00:14:52,590
Family comes first?

173
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:55,710
Your mother had to leave Winterfell

174
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:57,430
to protect the family.

175
00:14:57,430 --> 00:14:59,640
How can she protect the family

176
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:02,090
if she's not with her family?

177
00:15:03,060 --> 00:15:05,530
Your mother sat by your bed

178
00:15:05,530 --> 00:15:08,330
for three weeks while you slept...

179
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:10,290
And then she left!

180
00:15:12,350 --> 00:15:15,560
When you were born, I was the one  who pulled you from your mother.

181
00:15:16,530 --> 00:15:18,740
I placed you in her arms.

182
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:23,270
From that moment until the moment she dies,

183
00:15:24,070 --> 00:15:25,720
She will love you.

184
00:15:26,690 --> 00:15:28,360
Absolutely.

185
00:15:29,570 --> 00:15:32,840
- Fiercely. - Why did she leave?

186
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:34,860
I still can't tell you,

187
00:15:34,860 --> 00:15:36,470
but she will be home soon.

188
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:37,940
Do you know where she is now?

189
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:40,350
- Today? - No, I don't.

190
00:15:40,350 --> 00:15:43,340
Then how can you promise me she'll be home soon?

191
00:15:45,710 --> 00:15:49,370
Sometimes I worry you're too smart for your own good.

192
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:52,860
I'll never shoot another arrow.

193
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,860
And where is that written?

194
00:15:56,370 --> 00:15:58,830
You need legs to work a bow.

195
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:01,760
If the saddle Lord Tyrion designed actually works,

196
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:04,140
you could learn to shoot a bow from horseback.

197
00:16:04,220 --> 00:16:05,510
Really?

198
00:16:06,950 --> 00:16:09,730
Dothraki boys learn when they're four years old.

199
00:16:09,730 --> 00:16:11,240
Why shouldn't you?

200
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:28,500
Shh, keep it down.

201
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:31,410
You're not supposed to be inside the castle walls.

202
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:34,780
I thought you were supposed to be an important person around here.

203
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:37,090
Important enough for the likes of you.

204
00:16:38,190 --> 00:16:40,870
You're not the only nobleman in my life, you know.

205
00:16:40,870 --> 00:16:42,350
Who, the Imp?

206
00:16:42,450 --> 00:16:44,190
I'd call him half a nobleman.

207
00:16:44,190 --> 00:16:45,560
Jealous?

208
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:48,240
Why should I be jealous?

209
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:50,910
Anyone with a few coppers in his pocket can own you for the night.

210
00:16:52,010 --> 00:16:54,480
What's a dwarf like down below?

211
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:56,370
I've always wondered.

212
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:59,080
Might surprise you.

213
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:02,340
He's good with his fingers too.

214
00:17:02,630 --> 00:17:04,350
And his tongue.

215
00:17:05,140 --> 00:17:06,830
Generous tipper.

216
00:17:07,110 --> 00:17:09,720
I guess gold is cheap for a Lannister.

217
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:11,890
You are jealous.

218
00:17:12,010 --> 00:17:13,640
I'm a Greyjoy.

219
00:17:13,750 --> 00:17:15,950
We've been lords of the Iron Islands for 300 years.

220
00:17:15,950 --> 00:17:18,820
There's not a family in Westeros that can look down on us,

221
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:21,100
not even the Lannisters.

222
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:23,190
And what about the Starks?

223
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:27,570
I've been Lord Stark's ward since I was eight years old.

224
00:17:27,570 --> 00:17:30,830
A ward... that's a nice word for it.

225
00:17:30,830 --> 00:17:32,570
Your father rebelled against King Robert

226
00:17:32,570 --> 00:17:34,890
- and if he does it again... - My father fought

227
00:17:34,890 --> 00:17:37,100
for the freedom of his people.

228
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:38,730
What did your father do?

229
00:17:38,730 --> 00:17:40,910
Fucked a cook and whelped a whore.

230
00:17:40,910 --> 00:17:43,420
You're a very serious boy.

231
00:17:43,630 --> 00:17:47,000
- I'm not a boy. - Oh yes, you are.

232
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:51,290
A serious boy with a serious cock.

233
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:53,740
I don't want to pay for it.

234
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:56,640
Then get yourself a wife.

235
00:18:00,110 --> 00:18:01,320
Come on.

236
00:18:03,530 --> 00:18:05,270
I'm not gonna hurt you.

237
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:15,160
How is your son, my lord?

238
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:18,120
He'll never walk again.

239
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:22,410
But his mind is sound?

240
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:24,830
So they say.

241
00:18:25,690 --> 00:18:27,250
A blessing then.

242
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:32,040
I suffered an early mutilation myself.

243
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:36,480
Some doors close forever...

244
00:18:37,010 --> 00:18:40,830
Others open in the most unexpected places.

245
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:43,460
May I?

246
00:18:48,250 --> 00:18:51,380
If the wrong ears heard what I'm about to tell you,

247
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,240
off comes my head.

248
00:18:53,630 --> 00:18:56,200
And who would mourn poor Varys then?

249
00:18:56,200 --> 00:19:00,180
North or south, they sing no songs for spiders.

250
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:02,810
But there are things you must know.

251
00:19:03,060 --> 00:19:05,980
You are the King's Hand and the King is a fool...

252
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:07,970
your friend, I know, but a fool...

253
00:19:07,970 --> 00:19:10,820
And doomed unless you save him.

254
00:19:10,830 --> 00:19:13,480
I've been in the capital a month.

255
00:19:14,510 --> 00:19:17,370
Why have you waited so long to tell me this?

256
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:19,480
I didn't trust you.

257
00:19:19,890 --> 00:19:21,940
So why do you trust me now?

258
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:23,890
The Queen is not the only one

259
00:19:23,890 --> 00:19:26,380
who has been watching you closely.

260
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:29,070
There are few men of honor in the capital.

261
00:19:29,070 --> 00:19:30,640
You are one of them.

262
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:32,490
I would like to believe I am another,

263
00:19:32,490 --> 00:19:34,810
strange as that may seem.

264
00:19:34,810 --> 00:19:37,310
What sort of doom does the King face?

265
00:19:37,310 --> 00:19:40,220
The same sort as Jon Arryn.

266
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:44,160
The Tears of Lys, they call it.

267
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:46,620
A rare and costly thing,

268
00:19:46,670 --> 00:19:48,530
As clear and tasteless as water.

269
00:19:48,530 --> 00:19:50,330
It leaves no trace.

270
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:01,240
Who gave it to him?

271
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:04,710
Some dear friend, no doubt. But which one?

272
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:06,210
There were many.

273
00:20:06,210 --> 00:20:09,080
Lord Arryn was a kind and trusting man.

274
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:11,420
There was one boy.

275
00:20:11,430 --> 00:20:14,110
All he was he owed to Jon Arryn.

276
00:20:14,850 --> 00:20:16,900
The squire, Ser Hugh?

277
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:21,080
Pity what happened to him,

278
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:24,190
just when his life seemed to be going so nicely.

279
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:27,960
If Ser Hugh poisoned him...

280
00:20:29,630 --> 00:20:31,520
who paid Ser Hugh?

281
00:20:32,820 --> 00:20:34,710
Someone who could afford it.

282
00:20:34,710 --> 00:20:36,540
Jon was a man of peace.

283
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:39,210
He was Hand for 17 years...

284
00:20:39,210 --> 00:20:41,050
17 good years.

285
00:20:41,190 --> 00:20:42,820
Why kill him?

286
00:20:43,970 --> 00:20:47,330
He started asking questions.

287
00:21:16,470 --> 00:21:19,250
He's found one bastard already.

288
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:20,800
He has the book.

289
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,950
The rest will come.

290
00:21:23,030 --> 00:21:25,440
And when he knows the truth, what will he do?

291
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:27,320
The gods alone know.

292
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:29,900
The fools tried to kill his son.

293
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:33,620
What's worse... they botched it.

294
00:21:35,650 --> 00:21:38,610
The wolf and the lion will be at each other's throats.

295
00:21:39,030 --> 00:21:42,820
- We will be at war soon, my friend. - What good is war now?

296
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:44,170
We're not ready.

297
00:21:44,670 --> 00:21:47,310
If one Hand can die, why not a second?

298
00:21:47,310 --> 00:21:49,740
This Hand is not the other.

299
00:21:50,070 --> 00:21:51,580
We need time.

300
00:21:51,580 --> 00:21:55,020
Khal Drogo will not make his move until his son is born.

301
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:56,520
You know how these savages are.

302
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:58,790
"Delay," You say.

303
00:21:58,790 --> 00:22:00,340
"Move fast," I reply.

304
00:22:00,340 --> 00:22:03,740
This is no longer a game for two players.

305
00:22:03,850 --> 00:22:05,550
It never was.

306
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,480
The first to arrive and the last to leave.

307
00:22:29,740 --> 00:22:32,180
I admire your industry.

308
00:22:32,180 --> 00:22:34,330
You do move quietly.

309
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:37,320
We all have our qualities.

310
00:22:38,570 --> 00:22:40,580
You look a bit lonely today.

311
00:22:40,580 --> 00:22:42,930
You should pay a visit to my brothel this evening.

312
00:22:42,930 --> 00:22:44,760
First boy is on the house.

313
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:46,850
I think you're mistaking business with pleasure.

314
00:22:46,850 --> 00:22:48,020
Am I?

315
00:22:50,180 --> 00:22:52,320
All those birds that whisper in your ear...

316
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:54,310
such pretty little things.

317
00:22:55,630 --> 00:22:56,850
Trust me,

318
00:22:58,290 --> 00:23:00,810
we accommodate all inclinations.

319
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:02,540
Oh, I'm sure.

320
00:23:02,540 --> 00:23:05,870
Lord Redwyne likes his boys very young, I hear.

321
00:23:05,870 --> 00:23:09,280
I'm a purveyor of beauty and discretion...

322
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:11,000
both equally important.

323
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:14,930
Though I suppose beauty is a subjective quality, no?

324
00:23:15,390 --> 00:23:20,180
Is it true that Ser Marlon of Tumblestone prefers amputees?

325
00:23:20,180 --> 00:23:22,950
All desires are valid to a man with a full purse.

326
00:23:22,950 --> 00:23:26,550
And I heard the most awful rumor about a certain lord

327
00:23:26,550 --> 00:23:29,120
with a taste for fresh cadavers.

328
00:23:29,150 --> 00:23:32,980
Must be enormously difficult to accommodate that inclination.

329
00:23:32,980 --> 00:23:34,850
The logistics alone...

330
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:37,920
to find beautiful corpses before they rot.

331
00:23:37,920 --> 00:23:40,400
Strictly speaking, such a thing

332
00:23:40,400 --> 00:23:42,940
would not be in accordance with the King's laws.

333
00:23:42,940 --> 00:23:44,540
Strictly speaking.

334
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:50,220
Tell me... does someone somewhere

335
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:52,800
keep your balls in a little box?

336
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:55,750
I've often wondered.

337
00:23:57,660 --> 00:23:59,470
Do you know I have no idea where they are?

338
00:23:59,470 --> 00:24:01,950
And we had been so close.

339
00:24:03,290 --> 00:24:05,130
But enough about me. How have you been

340
00:24:05,130 --> 00:24:07,190
since we last saw each other?

341
00:24:07,190 --> 00:24:10,320
Since you last saw me or since I last saw you?

342
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:11,890
Now the last time I saw you,

343
00:24:11,890 --> 00:24:13,410
you were talking to the Hand of the King.

344
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:16,410
- Saw me with your own eyes? - Eyes I own.

345
00:24:16,410 --> 00:24:18,150
Council business.

346
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:21,140
We all have so much to discuss with Ned Stark.

347
00:24:21,140 --> 00:24:24,540
Everyone's well aware of your enduring fondness

348
00:24:24,540 --> 00:24:26,550
for Lord Stark's wife.

349
00:24:26,950 --> 00:24:30,580
If the Lannisters were behind the attempt on the Stark boy's life

350
00:24:30,580 --> 00:24:31,700
and it was discovered that

351
00:24:31,700 --> 00:24:35,150
you helped the Starks come to that conclusion...

352
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:39,580
to think a simple word to the Queen...

353
00:24:39,580 --> 00:24:41,710
One shudders at the thought.

354
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:44,420
But you know something? I do believe that I have seen you

355
00:24:44,420 --> 00:24:46,550
even more recently than you have seen me.

356
00:24:46,550 --> 00:24:48,600
- Have you? - Yes.

357
00:24:48,990 --> 00:24:51,090
Earlier today, I distinctly recall

358
00:24:51,090 --> 00:24:53,870
seeing you talking to Lord Stark in his chambers.

359
00:24:53,870 --> 00:24:55,800
Was that you under the bed?

360
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:57,690
And not long after that

361
00:24:57,690 --> 00:25:00,200
when I saw you escorting a certain

362
00:25:00,990 --> 00:25:03,350
foreign dignitary...

363
00:25:03,870 --> 00:25:05,660
Council business?

364
00:25:06,190 --> 00:25:09,540
Of course you would have friends from across the Narrow Sea.

365
00:25:09,540 --> 00:25:12,180
You're from there yourself, after all.

366
00:25:12,190 --> 00:25:15,480
We're friends, aren't we, Lord Varys?

367
00:25:15,730 --> 00:25:17,660
I'd like to think we are.

368
00:25:17,710 --> 00:25:20,100
So you can imagine my burden,

369
00:25:20,290 --> 00:25:24,360
wondering if the king might question my friend's sympathies.

370
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:25,830
To stand at a crossroads

371
00:25:25,830 --> 00:25:28,290
where turning left means loyalty to a friend,

372
00:25:28,290 --> 00:25:30,360
turning right loyalty to the realm...

373
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:32,640
- Please. - Define myself in a position

374
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:34,840
where a simple word to the king...

375
00:25:34,840 --> 00:25:36,840
What are you two conspiring about?

376
00:25:37,530 --> 00:25:39,690
Well, whatever it is, you'd best hurry up.

377
00:25:40,550 --> 00:25:41,880
My brother is coming.

378
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:43,650
To a small council meeting?

379
00:25:43,650 --> 00:25:46,320
Disturbing news from far away.

380
00:25:47,590 --> 00:25:49,000
Haven't you heard?

381
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:21,270
Off with you. No begging.

382
00:26:21,270 --> 00:26:22,930
I'm not a beggar. I live here.

383
00:26:22,930 --> 00:26:25,270
Do you want a smack on your ear to help you with your hearing?

384
00:26:25,270 --> 00:26:26,890
I want to see my father.

385
00:26:26,890 --> 00:26:29,300
I want to fuck the queen, for all the good it does me.

386
00:26:30,080 --> 00:26:31,760
You want your father, boy?

387
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:34,160
He's lying on the floor of some tavern,

388
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:36,250
getting pissed on by his friends.

389
00:26:36,250 --> 00:26:38,180
My father is Hand of the King!

390
00:26:38,450 --> 00:26:41,220
I'm not a boy. I'm Arya Stark of Winterfell

391
00:26:41,220 --> 00:26:42,380
and if you lay a hand on me,

392
00:26:42,380 --> 00:26:44,760
my father will have both your heads on spikes.

393
00:26:44,760 --> 00:26:46,130
Now are you going to let me by

394
00:26:46,130 --> 00:26:49,630
or do I need to smack you on the ear to help with your hearing?

395
00:26:52,170 --> 00:26:55,320
You know I had half my guard out searching for you?

396
00:26:58,510 --> 00:27:00,090
You promised me this would stop.

397
00:27:00,090 --> 00:27:02,020
They said they were going to kill you.

398
00:27:02,030 --> 00:27:04,250
- Who did? - I didn't see them,

399
00:27:04,450 --> 00:27:06,730
- but I think one was fat. - Oh, Arya.

400
00:27:06,740 --> 00:27:09,400
I'm not lying! They said you found the bastard

401
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:12,190
and the wolves are fighting the lions and the savage...

402
00:27:12,450 --> 00:27:14,240
something about the savage.

403
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:15,880
Where did you hear this?

404
00:27:15,880 --> 00:27:18,270
In the dungeons, near the dragon skulls.

405
00:27:18,270 --> 00:27:19,810
What were you doing in the dungeons?

406
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:22,660
Chasing a cat.

407
00:27:25,710 --> 00:27:26,990
Pardon, my lord.

408
00:27:26,990 --> 00:27:29,050
There's a night's watchman here begging a word.

409
00:27:29,050 --> 00:27:30,480
He says it's urgent.

410
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:40,370
- Your name, friend? - Yoren, if it please.

411
00:27:41,310 --> 00:27:43,730
This must be your son. He has the look.

412
00:27:43,730 --> 00:27:44,370
I'm a girl!

413
00:27:44,370 --> 00:27:46,080
Did Benjen send you?

414
00:27:46,080 --> 00:27:47,790
No one sent me, my lord.

415
00:27:47,820 --> 00:27:50,060
I'm here to find men for the Wall,

416
00:27:50,100 --> 00:27:53,420
see if there's any scum in the dungeons that might be fit for service.

417
00:27:53,740 --> 00:27:55,460
Oh, we'll find recruits for you.

418
00:27:55,460 --> 00:27:56,380
Thank you, my lord.

419
00:27:56,380 --> 00:27:58,770
But that's not why I disturb you now.

420
00:28:00,130 --> 00:28:03,430
Your brother Benjen, his blood runs black...

421
00:28:03,430 --> 00:28:05,700
makes him as much my brother as yours.

422
00:28:06,180 --> 00:28:08,130
It's for his sake I rode here so hard

423
00:28:08,130 --> 00:28:10,110
I damn near killed my horse.

424
00:28:10,670 --> 00:28:12,720
There are others riding too.

425
00:28:12,880 --> 00:28:15,060
The whole city will know by tomorrow.

426
00:28:15,070 --> 00:28:16,330
Know what?

427
00:28:17,830 --> 00:28:20,010
Best said in private, my lord.

428
00:28:25,980 --> 00:28:28,370
Go on. We'll talk more later.

429
00:28:29,630 --> 00:28:31,740
Jory, take her safely to her room.

430
00:28:32,040 --> 00:28:34,400
Come along, my lady. You heard your father.

431
00:28:40,550 --> 00:28:42,440
How many guards does my father have?

432
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:44,390
Here in King's Landing? 50.

433
00:28:45,370 --> 00:28:47,920
You wouldn't let anyone kill him, would you?

434
00:28:48,100 --> 00:28:50,600
No fear on that count, little lady.

435
00:28:55,710 --> 00:28:58,910
- Well? - It's about your wife, my lord.

436
00:29:00,870 --> 00:29:02,720
She's taken the Imp.

437
00:29:19,330 --> 00:29:21,300
You're far from home, Lady Stark.

438
00:29:21,300 --> 00:29:22,980
To whom do I speak?

439
00:29:22,980 --> 00:29:25,550
Ser Vardis Egen, Knight of the Vale.

440
00:29:26,020 --> 00:29:28,010
Is Lady Arryn expecting your visit?

441
00:29:28,010 --> 00:29:30,170
There was no time to send word.

442
00:29:30,220 --> 00:29:31,940
May I ask, my lady,

443
00:29:32,440 --> 00:29:34,440
why he is with you?

444
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:36,920
That's why there was no time.

445
00:29:37,030 --> 00:29:39,850
- He is my prisoner. - He doesn't look like a prisoner.

446
00:29:39,850 --> 00:29:42,980
My sister will decide what he looks like.

447
00:29:43,690 --> 00:29:45,130
Yes, my lady.

448
00:29:45,160 --> 00:29:46,570
She will at that.

449
00:29:53,080 --> 00:29:56,730
The Eyrie. They say it's impregnable.

450
00:29:57,610 --> 00:30:00,310
Give me 10 good men and some climbing spikes...

451
00:30:00,310 --> 00:30:02,250
I'll impregnate the bitch.

452
00:30:03,400 --> 00:30:04,590
I like you.

453
00:30:15,300 --> 00:30:18,680
Lord Stark, your presence has been requested in the small council chamber.

454
00:30:18,690 --> 00:30:19,660
A meeting has been called.

455
00:30:19,670 --> 00:30:22,290
I need to see the king first... alone.

456
00:30:22,300 --> 00:30:24,010
The king is at the small council meeting, my lord.

457
00:30:24,020 --> 00:30:25,330
He has summoned you.

458
00:30:26,310 --> 00:30:29,370
- Is it about my wife? - No, my lord.

459
00:30:29,390 --> 00:30:31,930
I believe it concerns Daenerys Targaryen.

460
00:30:32,130 --> 00:30:34,820
The whore is pregnant.

461
00:30:34,830 --> 00:30:36,510
You're speaking of murdering a child.

462
00:30:36,510 --> 00:30:40,310
I warned you this would happen. Back in the north, I warned you,

463
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:41,750
but you didn't care to hear.

464
00:30:41,760 --> 00:30:43,960
Well, hear it now.

465
00:30:44,980 --> 00:30:48,100
I want 'em dead, mother and child both.

466
00:30:48,110 --> 00:30:50,210
And that fool Viserys as well.

467
00:30:50,220 --> 00:30:51,830
Is that plain enough for you?

468
00:30:52,030 --> 00:30:53,560
I want them both dead.

469
00:30:53,570 --> 00:30:55,760
You will dishonor yourself forever if you do this.

470
00:30:55,770 --> 00:30:56,710
Honor?!

471
00:30:57,210 --> 00:30:59,760
I've got seven kingdoms to rule!

472
00:30:59,770 --> 00:31:02,770
One king, seven kingdoms.

473
00:31:02,870 --> 00:31:05,390
Do you think honor keeps them in line?

474
00:31:05,400 --> 00:31:07,650
Do you think it's honor that's keeping the peace?

475
00:31:07,660 --> 00:31:10,330
It's fear... fear and blood.

476
00:31:10,340 --> 00:31:11,780
Then we're no better than the Mad King.

477
00:31:11,790 --> 00:31:14,140
Careful, Ned. Careful now.

478
00:31:14,150 --> 00:31:15,800
You want to assassinate a girl

479
00:31:16,360 --> 00:31:18,110
because the spider heard a rumor?

480
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:21,100
No rumor, my lord. The princess is with child.

481
00:31:21,110 --> 00:31:22,720
Based on whose information?

482
00:31:22,730 --> 00:31:26,830
Ser Jorah Mormont. He is serving as advisor to the Targaryens.

483
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:29,090
Mormont? You bring us the whispers

484
00:31:29,100 --> 00:31:32,980
of a traitor half a world away and call it fact?

485
00:31:32,990 --> 00:31:35,700
Jorah Mormont's a slaver, not a traitor.

486
00:31:35,710 --> 00:31:38,310
Small difference, I know, to an honorable man.

487
00:31:38,320 --> 00:31:41,600
He broke the law, betrayed his family, fled our land.

488
00:31:41,940 --> 00:31:44,090
We commit murder on the word of this man?

489
00:31:44,100 --> 00:31:45,390
And if he's right?

490
00:31:45,680 --> 00:31:47,670
If she has a son?

491
00:31:47,830 --> 00:31:51,420
A Targaryen at the head of a Dothraki army...

492
00:31:51,430 --> 00:31:54,680
- What then? - The narrow sea still lies between us.

493
00:31:55,520 --> 00:31:56,610
I'll fear the Dothraki

494
00:31:56,610 --> 00:31:59,360
the day they teach their horses to run on water.

495
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:01,350
Do nothing?

496
00:32:01,490 --> 00:32:03,900
That's your wise advice?

497
00:32:03,910 --> 00:32:07,050
Do nothing till our enemies are on our shores?

498
00:32:07,570 --> 00:32:09,820
You're my council. Counsel!

499
00:32:09,830 --> 00:32:13,100
Speak sense to this honorable fool.

500
00:32:13,460 --> 00:32:17,700
I understand your misgivings, my lord.

501
00:32:17,710 --> 00:32:20,270
Truly, I do. It is a terrible thing

502
00:32:20,280 --> 00:32:22,630
we must consider, a vile thing.

503
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:25,630
Yet we who presume to rule must sometimes

504
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:29,370
do vile things for the good of the realm.

505
00:32:29,510 --> 00:32:32,630
Should the gods grant Daenerys a son,

506
00:32:32,770 --> 00:32:34,240
the realm will bleed.

507
00:32:34,560 --> 00:32:36,510
I bear this girl no ill will,

508
00:32:36,520 --> 00:32:38,760
but should the Dothraki invade,

509
00:32:38,770 --> 00:32:40,650
how many innocents will die?

510
00:32:40,660 --> 00:32:43,210
How many towns will burn?

511
00:32:43,220 --> 00:32:46,460
Is it not wiser, kinder even,

512
00:32:46,470 --> 00:32:48,320
that she should die now

513
00:32:48,520 --> 00:32:51,600
so that tens of thousands might live?

514
00:32:51,610 --> 00:32:53,770
We should have had them both killed years ago.

515
00:32:54,520 --> 00:32:56,920
When you find yourself in bed with an ugly woman,

516
00:32:56,930 --> 00:32:59,930
best close your eyes, get it over with.

517
00:33:00,390 --> 00:33:03,390
Cut her throat. Be done with it.

518
00:33:09,750 --> 00:33:11,630
I followed you into war...

519
00:33:12,410 --> 00:33:13,490
twice,

520
00:33:14,620 --> 00:33:15,970
without doubts,

521
00:33:16,670 --> 00:33:18,420
without second thoughts.

522
00:33:19,250 --> 00:33:21,240
But I will not follow you now.

523
00:33:22,490 --> 00:33:24,380
The Robert I grew up with

524
00:33:24,640 --> 00:33:28,200
didn't tremble at the shadow of an unborn child.

525
00:33:30,280 --> 00:33:31,970
She dies.

526
00:33:33,430 --> 00:33:35,060
I will have no part in it.

527
00:33:35,330 --> 00:33:37,770
You're the King's Hand, lord Stark.

528
00:33:37,780 --> 00:33:41,510
You'll do as I command or I'll find me a hand who will.

529
00:33:50,090 --> 00:33:51,360
And good luck to him.

530
00:33:52,450 --> 00:33:54,100
I thought you were a better man.

531
00:33:54,540 --> 00:33:56,610
Out. Out, damn you.

532
00:33:56,620 --> 00:33:58,300
I'm done with you.

533
00:33:59,110 --> 00:34:02,340
Go, run back to Winterfell!

534
00:34:02,350 --> 00:34:04,950
I'll have your head on a spike!

535
00:34:05,980 --> 00:34:09,240
I'll put it there myself, you fool!

536
00:34:09,250 --> 00:34:12,900
You think you're too good for this? Too proud and honorable?

537
00:34:12,910 --> 00:34:14,240
This is a war!

538
00:34:16,970 --> 00:34:18,550
I'll go ahead with my daughters.

539
00:34:18,560 --> 00:34:20,210
Get them ready. Do it yourself.

540
00:34:20,220 --> 00:34:22,530
- Don't ask anyone for help. - Right away, my lord.

541
00:34:22,980 --> 00:34:24,490
Lord Baelish is here for you.

542
00:34:26,860 --> 00:34:29,430
His grace went on about you at some length

543
00:34:29,440 --> 00:34:30,910
after you took your leave.

544
00:34:31,510 --> 00:34:33,280
The word "Treason" was mentioned.

545
00:34:34,830 --> 00:34:35,980
What can I do for you?

546
00:34:36,450 --> 00:34:37,970
When do you return to Winterfell?

547
00:34:38,150 --> 00:34:41,370
- Why? What do you care? - If you're still here come nightfall,

548
00:34:41,380 --> 00:34:42,350
I'll take you to see the last

549
00:34:42,360 --> 00:34:44,980
person Jon Arryn spoke with before falling ill.

550
00:34:44,990 --> 00:34:47,500
If that sort of thing still interests you.

551
00:34:48,450 --> 00:34:49,740
I don't have the time.

552
00:34:50,260 --> 00:34:52,620
It won't take more than an hour. But as you please.

553
00:34:58,850 --> 00:35:02,460
Round up all the men we have and station them outside the girls' chambers.

554
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:05,710
- Who are your best two swords? - Heward and Wyl.

555
00:35:05,720 --> 00:35:08,300
Find them and meet me at the stables.

556
00:35:14,060 --> 00:35:16,320
You bring him here without permission?

557
00:35:16,630 --> 00:35:19,790
You pollute my home with his presence?

558
00:35:22,210 --> 00:35:24,020
Your aunt has done a bad thing, Robin,

559
00:35:24,030 --> 00:35:25,710
A very bad thing.

560
00:35:26,700 --> 00:35:28,300
You remember her, don't you?

561
00:35:29,790 --> 00:35:31,100
Isn't he beautiful?

562
00:35:31,570 --> 00:35:34,610
And strong too. Jon knew it.

563
00:35:34,710 --> 00:35:37,700
His last words were "The seed is strong."

564
00:35:37,740 --> 00:35:39,060
He wanted everyone to know

565
00:35:39,070 --> 00:35:42,280
what a good, strong boy his son would grow up to be.

566
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:46,260
Look at him, the Lord of all the Vale.

567
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:51,090
Lysa, you wrote me about the Lannisters,

568
00:35:51,140 --> 00:35:54,100
- warning me... - To stay away from them!

569
00:35:54,140 --> 00:35:55,900
Not to bring one here!

570
00:35:57,290 --> 00:35:58,120
Mommy?

571
00:35:59,370 --> 00:36:02,180
- Is that the bad man? - It is.

572
00:36:04,520 --> 00:36:05,910
He's little.

573
00:36:07,100 --> 00:36:09,410
He's Tyrion the Imp of house Lannister.

574
00:36:10,170 --> 00:36:11,800
He killed your father.

575
00:36:11,810 --> 00:36:13,480
He murdered the Hand of the King!

576
00:36:13,490 --> 00:36:15,870
Oh, did I kill him too?

577
00:36:15,880 --> 00:36:17,980
I've been a very busy man.

578
00:36:17,990 --> 00:36:20,060
You will watch your tongue!

579
00:36:21,170 --> 00:36:22,980
These men are knights of the Vale.

580
00:36:23,530 --> 00:36:25,610
Every one of them loved Jon Arryn.

581
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:27,810
Every one of them would die for me.

582
00:36:27,820 --> 00:36:31,560
If any harm comes to me, my brother Jaime will see that they do.

583
00:36:31,570 --> 00:36:34,450
You can't hurt us. No one can hurt us here. Tell him, mommy!

584
00:36:34,460 --> 00:36:37,900
- Tell him! - shh shh shh, my sweet boy.

585
00:36:38,660 --> 00:36:40,620
He's just trying to frighten us.

586
00:36:41,110 --> 00:36:43,290
Lannisters are all liars.

587
00:36:43,380 --> 00:36:45,340
No one will hurt my baby.

588
00:36:45,890 --> 00:36:46,840
Mommy...

589
00:36:48,030 --> 00:36:50,930
I want to see the bad man fly.

590
00:36:53,060 --> 00:36:54,810
Perhaps you will, my little love.

591
00:36:54,820 --> 00:36:56,860
This man is my prisoner.

592
00:36:57,070 --> 00:36:59,200
I will not have him harmed.

593
00:37:01,690 --> 00:37:02,900
Ser Vardis,

594
00:37:03,580 --> 00:37:05,580
My sister's guest is weary.

595
00:37:06,410 --> 00:37:09,070
Take him down below so he can rest.

596
00:37:09,500 --> 00:37:11,210
Introduce him to Mord.

597
00:37:14,200 --> 00:37:15,700
You go sleep, dwarf man.

598
00:37:16,550 --> 00:37:18,480
Sleep good, little dwarf man!

599
00:37:54,400 --> 00:37:56,640
Lord Stark's lucky he still has a head.

600
00:37:57,050 --> 00:37:59,550
Robert will rant for a few days, but he won't do anything.

601
00:37:59,550 --> 00:38:00,680
He adores the man.

602
00:38:01,700 --> 00:38:03,180
You're jealous.

603
00:38:03,830 --> 00:38:05,210
Are you sure this won't hurt?

604
00:38:05,390 --> 00:38:07,070
Only if I slip.

605
00:38:10,650 --> 00:38:13,110
And you'd prefer me like this?

606
00:38:14,290 --> 00:38:16,710
If you want hairless, maybe you should find a little boy.

607
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:17,750
I want you.

608
00:38:19,610 --> 00:38:22,600
My brother thinks that anyone who hasn't been to war isn't a man.

609
00:38:22,940 --> 00:38:25,130
He treats me as if I'm a spoiled child.

610
00:38:27,100 --> 00:38:28,900
Oh, and you're not?

611
00:38:29,600 --> 00:38:32,110
Loras Tyrell, the Knight of the Fowers?

612
00:38:32,270 --> 00:38:33,900
How many wars have you fought in?

613
00:38:34,280 --> 00:38:37,740
Oh, and how much did your father spend on that armor of yours?

614
00:38:37,750 --> 00:38:38,970
Hold still.

615
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:42,170
All I ever hear from Robert and Stannis

616
00:38:42,170 --> 00:38:45,840
is how I'm not tough enough, how I squirm at the sight of blood...

617
00:38:45,850 --> 00:38:46,950
You did vomit when that boy's eye

618
00:38:46,960 --> 00:38:48,160
was knocked out in the melee.

619
00:38:48,170 --> 00:38:50,600
His eye was dangling out of the damn socket!

620
00:38:50,610 --> 00:38:51,620
He shouldn't have entered the melee

621
00:38:51,620 --> 00:38:52,710
if he didn't know how to fight.

622
00:38:52,720 --> 00:38:54,140
Easy for you to say.

623
00:38:54,230 --> 00:38:56,340
Not everyone is such a gifted swordsman.

624
00:38:56,350 --> 00:38:58,760
It's not a gift. No one gave it to me.

625
00:38:58,900 --> 00:39:00,580
I'm good because I work at it...

626
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:03,360
every day of my life since I could hold a stick.

627
00:39:04,070 --> 00:39:06,140
I could work at fighting all day, every day,

628
00:39:06,150 --> 00:39:08,030
and still never be as good as you.

629
00:39:08,040 --> 00:39:10,210
Yes well, I guess we'll never know.

630
00:39:20,290 --> 00:39:21,650
- Everywhere? - Everywhere.

631
00:39:22,940 --> 00:39:25,090
So how did it end up?

632
00:39:25,250 --> 00:39:26,870
The Targaryen girl will die?

633
00:39:26,910 --> 00:39:30,020
It needs to be done, unpleasant as it is.

634
00:39:30,460 --> 00:39:32,360
Robert's rather tasteless about it.

635
00:39:32,610 --> 00:39:34,000
Every time he talks about killing her,

636
00:39:34,010 --> 00:39:36,440
I swear the table rises six inches.

637
00:39:36,450 --> 00:39:39,280
It's a shame he can't muster the same enthusiasm for his wife.

638
00:39:39,290 --> 00:39:41,960
He does have a deep, abiding lust for her money.

639
00:39:42,300 --> 00:39:44,090
You have to give it to the Lannisters...

640
00:39:44,100 --> 00:39:46,050
they may be the most pompous, ponderous cunts

641
00:39:46,060 --> 00:39:47,470
the gods ever suffered to walk the world,

642
00:39:47,480 --> 00:39:49,940
but they do have outrageous amounts of money.

643
00:39:51,610 --> 00:39:53,650
I have an outrageous amount of money.

644
00:39:53,660 --> 00:39:55,830
Not as much as the Lannisters.

645
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:58,030
But a lot more than you.

646
00:39:59,640 --> 00:40:01,970
Robert's threatening to take me hunting with him.

647
00:40:02,590 --> 00:40:04,710
Last time we were out there for two weeks.

648
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:07,050
Tramping through the trees in the rain, day after day,

649
00:40:07,060 --> 00:40:10,010
all so he can stick his spear into something's flesh.

650
00:40:10,590 --> 00:40:13,740
Oh. But Robert loves his killing.

651
00:40:14,170 --> 00:40:15,970
And he's the king.

652
00:40:15,980 --> 00:40:19,280
- How did that ever happen? - Because he loves his killing.

653
00:40:19,540 --> 00:40:21,000
And he used to be good at it.

654
00:40:22,560 --> 00:40:23,940
Do you know who should be king?

655
00:40:25,480 --> 00:40:27,110
- Be serious. - I am.

656
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:29,690
My father could be your bank.

657
00:40:29,800 --> 00:40:32,960
I've never fought in a war before, but I'd fight for you.

658
00:40:32,970 --> 00:40:34,530
I'm fourth in line.

659
00:40:34,540 --> 00:40:37,270
And where was Robert in the line of royal succession?

660
00:40:37,700 --> 00:40:40,040
Joffrey is a monster. Tommen is eight.

661
00:40:40,050 --> 00:40:42,890
- Stannis? - Stannis has the personality of a lobster.

662
00:40:42,900 --> 00:40:44,730
He's still my older brother.

663
00:40:45,920 --> 00:40:47,300
- What are you doing?! - Look at it.

664
00:40:47,310 --> 00:40:49,050
- You cut me. - It's just blood.

665
00:40:49,050 --> 00:40:51,900
We've all got it in us. Sometimes a little spills.

666
00:40:52,690 --> 00:40:55,090
If you become king, you're going to see a lot of this.

667
00:40:55,400 --> 00:40:56,900
You need to get used to it.

668
00:40:57,700 --> 00:40:59,290
Go on. Look.

669
00:41:02,270 --> 00:41:03,970
People love you.

670
00:41:05,390 --> 00:41:07,460
They love to serve you because you're kind to them.

671
00:41:07,980 --> 00:41:09,300
They want to be near you.

672
00:41:12,210 --> 00:41:14,590
You're willing to do what needs to be done,

673
00:41:16,050 --> 00:41:17,710
but you don't gloat over it.

674
00:41:18,620 --> 00:41:20,300
You don't love killing.

675
00:41:23,070 --> 00:41:24,320
Where is it written that

676
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:27,680
power is the sole province of the worst?

677
00:41:28,750 --> 00:41:31,280
That Thrones are only made for

678
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:32,380
the hated and the feared?

679
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:38,680
You would be a wonderful king.

680
00:41:56,280 --> 00:41:59,290
I'm sorry your marriage to Ned Stark didn't work out.

681
00:41:59,640 --> 00:42:01,050
You seemed so good together.

682
00:42:01,380 --> 00:42:04,030
I'm glad I could do something to make you happy.

683
00:42:07,950 --> 00:42:10,570
Without a Hand, everything will fall to pieces.

684
00:42:11,140 --> 00:42:12,710
I suppose this is where you tell me

685
00:42:12,720 --> 00:42:15,540
to give the job to your brother Jaime.

686
00:42:15,740 --> 00:42:18,570
No. He's not serious enough.

687
00:42:20,210 --> 00:42:22,080
I'll say this for Ned Stark:

688
00:42:22,280 --> 00:42:23,770
he's serious enough.

689
00:42:24,520 --> 00:42:27,650
Was it really worth it? Losing him this way?

690
00:42:28,180 --> 00:42:29,120
I don't know.

691
00:42:32,680 --> 00:42:34,120
But I do know this:

692
00:42:35,310 --> 00:42:37,270
If the Targaryen girl convinces

693
00:42:37,270 --> 00:42:40,020
her horselord husband to invade

694
00:42:40,700 --> 00:42:43,970
and the Dothraki horde crosses the Narrow Sea...

695
00:42:46,080 --> 00:42:47,770
We won't be able to stop them.

696
00:42:47,880 --> 00:42:50,440
The Dothraki don't sail. Every child knows that.

697
00:42:50,450 --> 00:42:53,110
They don't have discipline. They don't have armor.

698
00:42:53,730 --> 00:42:55,340
They don't have siege weapons.

699
00:42:55,350 --> 00:42:57,250
It's a neat little trick you do:

700
00:42:57,260 --> 00:43:00,650
You move your lips and your father's voice comes out.

701
00:43:01,760 --> 00:43:03,000
Is my father wrong?

702
00:43:07,180 --> 00:43:09,880
Let's say Viserys Targaryen lands

703
00:43:09,890 --> 00:43:13,650
with 40,000 Dothraki screamers at his back.

704
00:43:13,650 --> 00:43:15,630
We hole up in our castles...

705
00:43:16,150 --> 00:43:18,780
A wise move... only a fool

706
00:43:18,790 --> 00:43:21,320
would meet the Dothraki in an open field.

707
00:43:22,260 --> 00:43:24,150
They leave us in our castles.

708
00:43:24,340 --> 00:43:28,500
They go from town to town, looting and burning,

709
00:43:28,510 --> 00:43:32,120
killing every man who can't hide behind a stone wall,

710
00:43:32,130 --> 00:43:34,890
stealing all our crops and livestock,

711
00:43:34,900 --> 00:43:37,260
enslaving all our women and children.

712
00:43:37,680 --> 00:43:40,230
How long do the people of the Seven Kingdoms stand behind

713
00:43:40,240 --> 00:43:43,620
their absentee king, their cowardly king

714
00:43:43,630 --> 00:43:46,070
hiding behind high walls?

715
00:43:46,120 --> 00:43:49,090
When do the people decide that Viserys Targaryen

716
00:43:49,100 --> 00:43:51,410
is the rightful monarch after all?

717
00:43:53,090 --> 00:43:54,400
We still outnumber them.

718
00:43:56,680 --> 00:44:00,030
Which is the bigger number: five or one?

719
00:44:01,420 --> 00:44:02,490
Five.

720
00:44:03,580 --> 00:44:04,650
Five...

721
00:44:07,180 --> 00:44:08,240
One.

722
00:44:09,160 --> 00:44:11,780
One army... a real army

723
00:44:11,790 --> 00:44:15,610
united behind one leader with one purpose.

724
00:44:17,190 --> 00:44:20,720
Our purpose died with the Mad King.

725
00:44:21,920 --> 00:44:24,110
Now we've got as many armies

726
00:44:24,160 --> 00:44:27,320
as there are men with gold in their purse.

727
00:44:27,840 --> 00:44:29,590
And everybody wants something different.

728
00:44:29,600 --> 00:44:32,130
Your father wants to own the world.

729
00:44:32,140 --> 00:44:35,610
Ned Stark wants to run away and bury his head in the snow.

730
00:44:35,620 --> 00:44:36,840
What do you want?

731
00:44:47,520 --> 00:44:51,080
We haven't had a real fight in nine years.

732
00:44:51,300 --> 00:44:53,580
Back-stabbing doesn't prepare you for a fight.

733
00:44:53,590 --> 00:44:55,650
And that's all the realm is now:

734
00:44:55,660 --> 00:44:57,870
back-stabbing and scheming

735
00:44:57,880 --> 00:45:00,460
and arse-licking and money-grubbing.

736
00:45:01,840 --> 00:45:02,710
Sometimes I don't know

737
00:45:02,710 --> 00:45:04,070
what holds it together.

738
00:45:05,550 --> 00:45:06,710
Our marriage.

739
00:45:16,970 --> 00:45:19,760
Ah, so here we sit

740
00:45:20,240 --> 00:45:22,460
17 years later,

741
00:45:22,780 --> 00:45:24,370
holding it all together.

742
00:45:25,860 --> 00:45:27,830
Don't you get tired?

743
00:45:28,320 --> 00:45:29,660
Every day.

744
00:45:31,810 --> 00:45:34,640
How long can hate hold a thing together?

745
00:45:34,690 --> 00:45:38,950
Well, 17 years is quite a long time.

746
00:45:39,760 --> 00:45:41,010
Yes, it is.

747
00:45:42,180 --> 00:45:43,230
Yes, it is.

748
00:45:49,260 --> 00:45:50,460
What was she like?

749
00:45:53,850 --> 00:45:56,280
You've never asked about her, not once.

750
00:45:56,280 --> 00:45:57,040
Why not?

751
00:45:58,610 --> 00:46:01,590
At first, just saying her name even in private

752
00:46:02,360 --> 00:46:04,760
felt like I was breathing life back into her.

753
00:46:06,360 --> 00:46:07,930
I thought if I didn't talk about her,

754
00:46:07,940 --> 00:46:10,280
she'd just fade away for you.

755
00:46:10,610 --> 00:46:12,580
When I realized that wasn't going to happen,

756
00:46:13,490 --> 00:46:15,640
I refused to ask out of spite.

757
00:46:16,460 --> 00:46:17,910
I didn't want to give you the satisfaction

758
00:46:17,920 --> 00:46:20,730
of thinking I cared enough to ask.

759
00:46:21,460 --> 00:46:22,330
And eventually it became

760
00:46:22,340 --> 00:46:24,780
clear that my spite didn't mean anything to you.

761
00:46:24,970 --> 00:46:27,220
As far as I could tell, you actually enjoyed it.

762
00:46:28,010 --> 00:46:29,370
So why now?

763
00:46:31,460 --> 00:46:35,320
What harm could Lyanna Stark's ghost do to either of us

764
00:46:35,940 --> 00:46:38,440
that we haven't done to each other a hundred times over?

765
00:46:42,760 --> 00:46:44,720
You want to know the horrible truth?

766
00:46:48,300 --> 00:46:50,600
I can't even remember what she looked like.

767
00:46:53,850 --> 00:46:58,200
I only know she was the one thing I ever wanted...

768
00:47:00,560 --> 00:47:02,370
Someone took her away from me,

769
00:47:04,380 --> 00:47:08,370
and seven kingdoms couldn't fill the hole she left behind.

770
00:47:12,540 --> 00:47:14,720
I felt something for you once, you know?

771
00:47:16,020 --> 00:47:17,110
I know.

772
00:47:18,510 --> 00:47:20,430
Even after we lost our first boy.

773
00:47:22,890 --> 00:47:24,830
For quite a while, actually.

774
00:47:29,100 --> 00:47:30,940
Was it ever possible for us?

775
00:47:30,950 --> 00:47:33,360
Was there ever a time, ever a moment?

776
00:47:40,770 --> 00:47:42,000
No.

777
00:47:46,370 --> 00:47:48,880
Does that make you feel better or worse?

778
00:47:53,820 --> 00:47:55,110
It doesn't make me feel anything.

779
00:48:10,820 --> 00:48:14,040
She looks like him, don't she, my Lord?

780
00:48:14,720 --> 00:48:17,570
She has his nose, his black hair.

781
00:48:18,900 --> 00:48:20,100
Aye.

782
00:48:20,390 --> 00:48:22,220
Tell him when you see him, my Lord.

783
00:48:22,390 --> 00:48:24,490
If it please you,

784
00:48:24,490 --> 00:48:26,830
tell him how beautiful she is.

785
00:48:28,470 --> 00:48:32,030
- I will. - And tell him I've been with no one else.

786
00:48:32,120 --> 00:48:35,200
I swear it, my lord, by the old gods and new.

787
00:48:35,680 --> 00:48:37,360
I don't want no jewels or nothing,

788
00:48:37,930 --> 00:48:38,770
just him.

789
00:48:39,640 --> 00:48:41,110
The king was always good to me.

790
00:48:41,690 --> 00:48:43,630
When Jon Arryn came to visit you,

791
00:48:44,390 --> 00:48:45,500
what did he want?

792
00:48:45,750 --> 00:48:47,530
He wasn't that sort of man, my lord.

793
00:48:48,000 --> 00:48:50,360
He just wanted to know if the child was happy,

794
00:48:50,880 --> 00:48:51,770
healthy.

795
00:48:55,830 --> 00:48:57,100
He looks healthy enough to me.

796
00:49:00,040 --> 00:49:01,480
The girl shall want for nothing.

797
00:49:08,100 --> 00:49:10,730
Brothels make a much better investment than ships,

798
00:49:10,740 --> 00:49:11,840
I've found.

799
00:49:12,070 --> 00:49:14,550
Whores rarely sink.

800
00:49:19,280 --> 00:49:21,900
What do you know of king Robert's bastards?

801
00:49:21,910 --> 00:49:24,390
Well, he has more than you,

802
00:49:24,390 --> 00:49:25,460
for a start.

803
00:49:25,850 --> 00:49:27,950
- How many? - Does it matter?

804
00:49:27,980 --> 00:49:29,680
If you fuck enough women,

805
00:49:29,680 --> 00:49:30,720
some of them will give you presents.

806
00:49:30,730 --> 00:49:33,170
And Jon Arryn tracked them all down. Why?

807
00:49:33,240 --> 00:49:34,380
He was the King's Hand.

808
00:49:34,380 --> 00:49:35,950
Perhaps Robert wanted them looked after.

809
00:49:35,960 --> 00:49:39,250
He was overcome with fatherly love.

810
00:49:42,460 --> 00:49:43,380
Come.

811
00:49:50,040 --> 00:49:51,680
- Jory! - My lord.

812
00:50:11,260 --> 00:50:13,350
Such a small pack of wolves.

813
00:50:14,980 --> 00:50:16,890
Stay back, ser. This is the Hand of the King.

814
00:50:16,900 --> 00:50:18,600
Was the Hand of the King.

815
00:50:19,230 --> 00:50:20,770
Now I'm not sure what he is...

816
00:50:20,780 --> 00:50:23,170
lord of somewhere very far away.

817
00:50:23,870 --> 00:50:25,640
What's the meaning of this, Lannister?

818
00:50:25,650 --> 00:50:28,040
Get back inside where it's safe.

819
00:50:28,360 --> 00:50:29,730
I'm looking for my brother.

820
00:50:29,890 --> 00:50:32,140
You remember my brother, don't you, Lord Stark?

821
00:50:32,180 --> 00:50:35,670
Blond hair, sharp tongue, short man.

822
00:50:36,650 --> 00:50:38,010
I remember him well.

823
00:50:38,020 --> 00:50:39,940
It seems he had some trouble on the road.

824
00:50:40,540 --> 00:50:42,510
You wouldn't know what happened to him, would you?

825
00:50:43,150 --> 00:50:45,240
He was taken at my command

826
00:50:45,570 --> 00:50:47,500
to answer for his crimes.

827
00:50:47,880 --> 00:50:49,240
My Lords!

828
00:50:50,620 --> 00:50:52,290
I'll bring the city watch.

829
00:50:54,510 --> 00:50:55,550
Come, Stark.

830
00:50:56,730 --> 00:50:58,410
I'd rather you die sword in hand.

831
00:50:58,420 --> 00:51:00,440
- If you threaten my Lord again... - Threaten?

832
00:51:00,690 --> 00:51:03,440
As in, "I'm going to open your lord

833
00:51:03,450 --> 00:51:06,730
from balls to brains and see what Starks are made of"?

834
00:51:07,310 --> 00:51:08,390
You kill me,

835
00:51:10,140 --> 00:51:11,510
your brother's a dead man.

836
00:51:12,600 --> 00:51:13,600
You're right.

837
00:51:14,440 --> 00:51:16,770
Take him alive. Kill his men.

838
00:52:52,420 --> 00:52:54,110
My brother, Lord Stark...

839
00:52:54,150 --> 00:52:55,230
we want him back.

